hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28182","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukayr ibn Abdillah, on the authority of al-Mundhir ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh narrated to him that she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him of blood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is only a vein, so look, when your menstruation comes, do not pray, and when the period passes, purify yourself, then pray between one period to the next."
"28183","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Sad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: My aunt Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh narrated to me, she said: I came to Aishah and said to her: O Mother of the Believers, I have feared that I have no share in Islam and that I am of the people of Fire, I remain what Allah wills of days in istihadah and I do not pray to Allah Almighty a prayer. She said: Sit until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) comes. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, she said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh, she fears she has no share in Islam and that she is of the people of Fire, she remains what Allah wills of days in istihadah and does not pray to Allah Almighty a prayer. He said: Command Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh to withhold each month the number of days of her periods, then wash and stuff and wrap and clean, then purify at every prayer and pray, for that is only a kick of Satan or a burst vein or a disease befalling her."
